TITLE:: RCLines
summary:: Sonic straight lines (glissandi in any parameters) and their generators: rails, tangents, projected surfaces, clouds
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCCurve, Classes/RCSurface, Classes/RCProjection, Classes/RCLineControl, Classes/RCSubseq

DESCRIPTION::
A uniform glissando is a straight line in the (time, pitch) plane; Xenakis drew the glissandi of emphasis::Metastasis:: as lines and read the ruled surfaces they sweep (emphasis::Formalized Music::, ch. I). RCLines takes the idea to a score space of time plus any number of named parameters, each linear in its own unit (pitch in octaves, amp in dB, azimuth in radians, a sample index...): a line is one note whose parameters glide from one end to the other. Generators return the lines of one cycle; link::Classes/RCLineControl:: hands them to the voices of a batch, and each voice's synth receives the ends as code::pitch0:: / code::pitch1::, code::amp0:: / code::amp1::... with code::sustain:: the line's length.

A line is an Event:
code::
(onset: 2, dur: 4, from: (pitch: 0, amp: -20), to: (pitch: 1, amp: -10), id: 3)
::
with, optionally, code::voice::, an Integer pinning the line to one voice of the batch (link::#*allocate::), and code::path::, a curved line's course that link::#*subseq:: hands to the voice per hit: an Event key → Env over the note (link::Classes/RCCurve::; a key without one is straight).
strong::onset:: and strong::dur:: in beats; strong::from:: and strong::to:: Events of the parameter values at the ends. A point of the score space is code::[time, params]::.

Every generator is pure and returns its lines in time order; the ones that draw are seeded.

CLASSMETHODS::

subsection:: Lines and points

METHOD:: line
A line.
argument:: onset
argument:: dur
argument:: from
argument:: to
argument:: id

METHOD:: between
The line from point strong::a:: to point strong::b:: (code::[time, params]::), in time order: when b comes first the ends are swapped. A line shorter than strong::minDur:: (vertical in the score: a chord) is stretched to minDur with its ends kept, a chirp.
argument:: a
argument:: b
argument:: minDur
Defaults to link::#*defaultMinDur::.
argument:: id

METHOD:: defaultMinDur
Beats; 0.01.

METHOD:: keysOf
The union of the parameter keys of the lines, sorted.

METHOD:: slope
The slope of a line for one key: units per beat.

METHOD:: lerpPoint
The point between two points at u (0 → a, 1 → b), key by key.

METHOD:: fromKey
METHOD:: toKey
METHOD:: paramKeys
The per-hit param names of a coordinate key (code::pitch:: → code::pitch0::, code::pitch1::) and the list a subseq of the given keys carries (the pairs, then code::sustain:: and code::line_id::).

subsection:: Rails: the string-art surfaces

METHOD:: rail
The affine rail from point a to point b: a Function u → point.

METHOD:: rails
strong::n:: lines, line i joining code::a.(u_i):: to code::b.(u_i):: for two rails (Functions u → point), u evenly spaced in [0, 1] or the given strong::us::. Two affine rails give the hyperbolic paraboloid of the string section of Metastasis (bars 309-314); a rail collapsed to one point (code::rail(p, p)::) gives the fan of its opening.

Curved rulings, a generalized ruled surface in the architect's sense: with strong::via:: (a point, or a rail u → point) each ruling is the quadratic Bézier arc from a.(u) to b.(u) pulled towards via.(u), strong::pull:: 0 the straight line, 1 the arc through via at its middle, more overshooting (a number, or an Event key → pull with code::\time:: for the time coordinate; a key it lacks stays straight). The arc's control point keeps its time between the ends', so its time stays monotone. strong::samples:: points along each arc (16); a curved line carries its code::path:: (link::Classes/RCCurve::).
code::
~a = RCLines.rail([0, (pitch: 0)], [0, (pitch: 2)]);   // at time 0, from pitch 0 to 2
~b = RCLines.rail([8, (pitch: 2)], [8, (pitch: 0)]);   // at time 8, the other way
RCLines.rails(~a, ~b, 12);                             // twelve crossing glissandi
RCLines.rails(~a, ~b, 12, via: [4, (pitch: 3)]);       // every string arching through pitch 3 at beat 4
::
argument:: a
argument:: b
argument:: n
argument:: us
argument:: minDur
argument:: via
argument:: pull
argument:: samples

subsection:: Tangents: the Xenakeur construction

METHOD:: tangents
Lines tangent to strong::curve:: (a Function tau → point) at the touch parameters strong::touches::. strong::extent:: says how far the line runs along the tangent, in units of tau: a number (each side), code::[before, after]::, or a Function code::(point, tangent, tau) → [before, after]:: (a buffer played at rate k lasts its length over k: the extent can follow the slope). strong::derivative::: a Function tau → code::[dtime, dparams]::, nil for central differences with strong::eps::.
code::
~curve = RCLines.parabola(4, (pitch: 1), 0.125);              // pitch = 1 + (t - 4)^2 / 8
RCLines.tangents(~curve, (0, 0.5 .. 8), [1, 1]);               // touches every half beat, two beats long
::

METHOD:: contact
Paths touching strong::curve:: at the touches, the tangential construction with bent generatrices: each path is the curve's tangent bent by strong::bend:: times half its second derivative, code::C(tau) + h C'(tau) + bend h²/2 C''(tau)::, h from -before to after (strong::extent:: as for link::#*tangents::). The curve is their envelope whatever the bend: 0 gives the tangent lines (exactly link::#*tangents::), 1 the osculating arcs (the curve to second order), 2 arcs curling past it: the mass moves from one side of the curve to the other through the curve itself. strong::bend::: a number, an Event key → number (the time coordinate reads code::\time::), or a Function tau → either. A bent path whose time turns back is cut at the turn (the part through the touch kept); its keys that stay straight carry no path (link::Classes/RCCurve#*lineFrom::).
code::
~curve = RCLines.parabola(4, (pitch: 1), 0.125);
RCLines.contact(~curve, (0, 0.5 .. 8), [1, 1], 1);             // the same touches, the arcs hugging the bowl
RCLines.contact(~curve, (0, 0.5 .. 8), [1, 1], (pitch: 2, az: 0));   // pitch curled inside, space straight
::
argument:: curve
argument:: touches
argument:: extent
argument:: bend
argument:: derivative
argument:: eps
argument:: minDur
argument:: samples
Points along each bent path (16).

METHOD:: parabola
The curve tau → code::[tau, apex + curvature * (tau - apexTime)^2]:: per key; strong::apex:: an Event (key → value at the apex), strong::curvature:: a number or an Event per key (units per beat², the sign turns it).

METHOD:: sine
A sine in any keys, tau → code::[tau, center + amp sin(2pi (tau - t0) / period + phase)]:: per key: strong::center:: and strong::amp:: Events (key → value), strong::period:: (beats) and strong::phase:: numbers or Events per key. Two keys a quarter turn apart in phase draw a helix (a spiral in pitch × az over time); other periods per key a Lissajous figure.
code::
~helix = RCLines.sine((pitch: 1, az: 0), (pitch: 0.5, az: 1), 8, (pitch: 0, az: 0.5pi));
RCLines.contact(~helix, (0, 0.5 .. 16), 1, 1);   // arcs hugging the spiral
::

METHOD:: circle
A circle (an ellipse) in the plane of time and the keys of strong::center::: tau an angle, the point code::[centerTime + radiusTime cos tau, center + radius sin tau]::. Its time turns back at tau = 0 and pi: link::#*contact:: cuts a path there.

METHOD:: spline
A smooth curve through the composer's points code::[[time, params], ...]:: (times increasing): cubic Hermite between them with the slopes of the neighbours (Catmull-Rom on uneven times, one-sided at the ends), tau the time; on along the end slopes outside. A key missing from a point is left out.

METHOD:: tangentAt
code::[point, tangent]:: of a curve at tau (numerical).

subsection:: Projected: a surface seen through a moving plane

METHOD:: projected
For each sample code::[u, v]:: of strong::surface:: (an link::Classes/RCSurface::), a segment or a curve of R^m through S(u, v), projected on the score space by strong::frame:: (an link::Classes/RCProjection::). strong::direction:::
list::
## code::\ruling:: the whole v-line of the sample, from vRange[0] to vRange[1] (on a ruled surface, the ruling itself)
## code::\u::, code::\v::, a number (an angle in the tangent plane, 0 = u, pi/2 = v) or a Function code::(u, v, i) → angle::: the tangent segment, bent by strong::bend:: times the surface's curvature along it (0 the tangent, 1 the geodesic to second order, 2 curling past it; a number or a Function code::(u, v, i) → number::)
## code::\geodesic:: the geodesic through the sample at strong::angle:: (a number or a Function code::(u, v, i) → angle::): the straightest curve on the surface
## code::\uLine::, code::\vLine:: the parameter line through the sample
## code::\gradient:: the steepest ascent of the frame's time through the sample, the line that climbs the score fastest (none at a critical point)
::
strong::length:: is the segment's or the curve's length in R^m, centred on the sample (ignored by code::\ruling::); a curve is drawn in strong::steps:: steps (about 1 ms per line at 12 steps in R^3). A curve whose time turns back is cut at the turn, the part through the sample kept, and fitted as a curved line (link::Classes/RCCurve#*lineFrom::). strong::timeMode::: code::\window:: keeps the lines starting within [0, cycle), code::\wrap:: wraps their onsets into the cycle, code::\sequence:: ignores the projected time and starts line i at i * cycle / n, code::\none:: keeps every line as projected. Each line remembers its code::sample:: and its code::ends::, the segment of R^m it was projected from, in the line's own order (the ends swap with the line when the second one comes first in time); a curved one also its code::curve::, its polyline in R^m in the same order.
code::
~s = RCSurface.hyperbolicParaboloid;
~p = RCProjection(3, [\pitch], scales: [8, 2]);   // time = 8 x beats, pitch = 2 y octaves
~p.rotate(1, 2, 0.3);                             // pitch reads some z too
RCLines.projected(~s, ~p, ~s.grid(6, 1), \ruling, timeMode: \wrap, cycle: 8);
// geodesics on a torus, and tangents hugging it
~t = RCSurface.torus(2, 1);
RCLines.projected(~t, ~p, ~t.random(12, 1), \geodesic, 3, \wrap, 8, angle: 0.3pi, steps: 12);
RCLines.projected(~t, ~p, ~t.random(12, 1), 0.3pi, 1, \wrap, 8, bend: 1);
::

subsection:: Sections: a surface cut by a moving hyperplane

METHOD:: sections
The slice of strong::surface:: by the moving hyperplane of strong::frame::'s time (or the hypersurface of strong::timeFunc::, a Function of R^m → number): at beat t of the cycle it is code::{T = offset + speed t}::, and what sounds is the slice. Strands stay on it, riding the surface's steepest ascent of T at unit time (link::Classes/RCSurface#-flow::), each a curved line whose time is exactly the score's (each sample's time is its point's) and whose other coordinates are the frame's projection of its point.
argument:: seeding
code::\slice:: (strong::n:: strands spread by arc length along the slice at the cycle's start, brought onto it by Newton steps), code::\births:: (n strands leaving every way from each bottom of T the hyperplane reaches in the cycle), code::\sweep:: (both), code::\random:: (n strands from random points the hyperplane crosses in the cycle; strong::seed::).
argument:: length
A strand ends at a top of T (where strands converge), at the edge of a patch, after strong::length:: beats or at the cycle's end: the strands live within a cycle.
argument:: speed
T units per beat; negative sweeps down (births at the tops).
argument:: steps
A whole cycle's strand (a shorter one fewer, at least 8).
argument:: res
The grid of the slice (the bottoms are found on one of half as many nodes).
returns:: The lines in time order, each with its R^m code::curve:: and code::ends::, its seed code::sample:: and how it was code::born:: (code::\slice::, code::\min::, code::\max::, code::\random::).
code::
~t = RCSurface.torus(2, 1);
~p = RCProjection(3, [\pitch, \az], scales: [1, 0.5, pi]);   // T = x
RCLines.sections(~t, ~p, -3.5, 0.75, 8, cycle: 8);           // born at the bottom, past both saddles by the cycle's end
::

subsection:: Cloud: Pithoprakta

METHOD:: cloud
strong::n:: short lines over one cycle: onsets uniform in [0, cycle), start values uniform in strong::ranges:: (key → [lo, hi]), speeds from Xenakis' law for glissando speeds (Formalized Music p. 14): |v| half-normal with temperature a, either sign, i.e. v ~ N(0, a / sqrt 2), units per beat, per key (strong::temperatures::: key → a; a key missing there is static). strong::dur::: a number or [min, max] (uniform), beats. With strong::clip::, an end leaving its range is clipped to it. strong::seed::: the same seed gives the same cloud.

subsection:: Voices

METHOD:: allocate
Distribute lines over strong::n:: voices, in onset order: code::\round_robin:: (line i to voice i mod n, overlaps allowed), code::\free:: (the voice free the longest; when every voice is busy, the one free soonest: an overlap on that voice), code::\strict:: (as free, but a line finding no free voice is dropped: n strings play at most n lines at once). A line carrying code::voice:: (an Integer) is pinned to voice code::voice mod n:: in every mode, placed first and never dropped: the thread of a continuous texture stays on one voice, and the free lines avoid that voice while it is busy. Returns code::(voices: Array of n Arrays of lines, dropped: Integer)::.

METHOD:: subseq
One voice's lines as an link::Classes/RCSubseq:: for the seq machinery (link::Classes/RCOrgnsmPatterns#*seqParams::): shift = the first onset, each hit lasting until the next line of the voice (the last one its own length), params code::key0:: / code::key1:: per line for every key of strong::keys:: (the lines' union when nil; a key a line lacks is nil there), plus code::sustain:: (the line's length) and code::line_id::. A line starting less than strong::minGap:: after the previous one of the voice is dropped (warned). nil for no lines.

EXAMPLES::
code::
// a cloud, allocated to eight strings
~lines = RCLines.cloud(30, 8, (pitch: [-1, 2], az: [-pi, pi]), (pitch: 1.5, az: 0.5), [0.5, 2], seed: 3);
~voices = RCLines.allocate(~lines, 8, \strict);
~voices[\dropped];
~voices[\voices].collect { |ls| RCLines.subseq(ls, [\az, \pitch]) };
::
